{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014x2ZAGS43w6HLFfwz2eDzB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the project documents, here's what Anchor **is**:\n\n- **A personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty** â€” a single-folder app at `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no siblings) that manages tasks, projects, and ideas across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing).\n\n- **Markdown is the source of truth.** All state lives in plain-text files â€” `DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, plus archives (`CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`). No database, no lock files, no binary formats.\n\n- **It ships two interfaces over the same logic:**\n  - `anchor_gui.py` â€” a self-contained, stdlib-only Python HTTP server + browser dashboard (the primary interface), running persistently on `http://localhost:8777` under the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. It reads/writes the markdown directly and supports a full task lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved â†’ restored).\n  - `anchor.py` â€” a CLI mirror that performs the same operations and regenerates the static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It guards its own health.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5 AM daily via Task Scheduler â€” a self-test that parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and state transition, and writes a dated report.\n\n- **It has grown a substantial \"R&D Control Surface\" (v2 â†’ v4).** Beyond task tracking, Anchor now hosts a \"Project Cockpit\" for **trio-driven R&D** â€” each project gets a window where the research â†’ planning â†’ build trio (researchPrime Â· Crucible Â· Foreman) runs as **persistent, isolated, server-side terminal sessions** managed like stacking windows. Key capabilities:\n  - **Real ConPTY terminals** (`pty_manager.py` / `terminal_session.py`) via the one declared native exception, `pywinpty` (lazy, optional `pip install .[terminal]` extra) â€” everything else stays stdlib-only.\n  - **Per-session git-worktree isolation**, a durable session registry, status-colored lights (green/amber/red/grey).\n  - **Cached, validated, grounding-filtered summaries** (session + project level) generated through a stubbable runner seam â€” never live `claude` in tests.\n  - A **session model** (one trio run = one session), a **Grass Catchers** idea lane, **deliverable pin/declare + launch-by-type**, stage **handoffs**, and an ephemeral **deliverable preview server** (hard-guarded off port 8777).\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built, 637 tests passing, merged to master 2026-06-13) adds: skill auto-load-once/greet-once (killing a repeating-prompt bug), a claudeâ†”gemini engine toggle, inline expanding lane panels, per-lane doc roles, and a cost/tokens/time rollup.\n\n- **Branding:** the dashboard presents as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" using a vendored brand mark.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: these claims come from `CLAUDE.md` and the locked planning docs (the design's own description). If you want me to verify any specific claim against the actual code (e.g., that the v4 endpoints exist or the tests really pass), I can check the source directly."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4789,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"09cf75cc-8a19-49c9-961e-54440729383b","uuid":"d1e73ae0-0214-46f5-8113-ed4163c2e8db","request_id":"req_011Cc1JMKjsfBuekxNSkDnRL"}
